From d8d00f94c73429a2e6870df7d0420fd70b1aa473 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncanmcqueen <206344294+duncanmcqueen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:09:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Haiku peer: draw shapes and images with native code

On Kaffe's interpreter, per-pixel Java code is very slow. Draw the
common cases natively, directly in the int[] pixels of the image:
rectangles, 1-pixel lines, any path (curves flattened, both winding
rules, with or without anti-aliasing), thin outlines as 1-pixel lines,
solid colours and linear gradients, images through any affine transform
(nearest neighbour or bilinear), and copyArea. Other cases (clips that
are not rectangles, texture paints, other composite rules) use the Java
code of AbstractGraphics2D as before.

Measured on Kaffe (microseconds per operation, before / after):
fillRect 100x100 1065 / 30, fillOval 7350 / 650, line of width 4
42100 / 310, gradient fill 160600 / 250, translucent image 16730 / 170,
scaled image 327720 / 580, rotated image 2965950 / 200,
copyArea 207620 / 60.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
